// Perishing: food that keeps for so long once it is made, then spoils
// (VILLAGE.md decision 8, slice 8).
//
// Cut points:
// - full:     food that is perishable (`keepsFor` more than 0: meat, a
//             meal) spoils at a time set as it is made: made, it keeps
//             that long; cooked, a meal keeps its `mealKeepsFor` from then,
//             whatever it was made of. That time is all there is: nothing
//             steps it, and nothing changes until it comes. Then the food
//             is spoiled food, as heavy, where it was: no longer food, so
//             nobody eats it. Food that keeps (grain, turnips) never
//             spoils. Salting and smoking are left out.
// - reduced:  the same.
// - abstract: the same: it needs no agent.
// - frozen:   the same: meat in a larder nobody is near spoils all the
//             same.
// - perception: what spoils is seen to be gone, and spoiled food there,
//             as anything made or ended is: by whoever sees it then, or
//             looks later. When it will spoil is not seen.
// - stacks:   a stack spoils whole, at once. Put with a stack of its unit
//             and merged, the two spoil at their times averaged, each
//             weighed by its mass: fresh meat buys older meat time, and
//             old meat costs fresh meat some.
// - hunger:   spoiled food isn't food (hunger/eating.tri's #Food), and is
//             made of rot (things.tri): no method finds it to eat, eating
//             it isn't possible, and nobody values it as food.
// - cooking:  cooking makes a meal of raw food (cooking/): it keeps its
//             `mealKeepsFor` from then.
// - code:     the perishing domain (src/domains_perishing.odin): it stamps
//             food made at the last boundary with when it spoils, and its
//             horizon is the next food to spoil, its one wake then.
//             effect_cook sets a meal's; spoiling is carved, as death's
//             remains are (src/act_actions.odin's `become`); a merge
//             averages (src/kinds_body_kind.odin).

package perishing

// What perishes: how long it keeps once made (0: it keeps, and never
// spoils); when it spoils (0: not yet known, or never), set as it is made;
// and what it becomes, spoiled ("": nothing, it rots away).
#Perishable: {
    @component(Perishable)
    keepsFor: *0ms | time & >=0ms & <=100d     @field(content, saved, inspect)
    spoilsAt: *0ms | time & >=0ms & <=10000d   @field(saved, proposable, inspect)
    spoiled:  *"spoiled_food" | text           @field(content, saved, inspect)
}

// Food perishes; a meal made of it keeps so long from when it is cooked.
hunger.#Food: #Perishable & {
    mealKeepsFor: *2d | time & >=0ms & <=100d  @field(content, saved, inspect)
}

// Spoiled: what was food (or a carcass, hunting/), gone off. It isn't
// food, nor made of it (things.tri's "rot", no kind of food): eating takes
// something made of food (hunger/eating.tri), and nobody values it as food.
// It rots away to nothing in ten days, wherever it is.
#Spoiled: #Body & #Perishable & { keepsFor: 10d, spoiled: "" }

spoiled_seen: #Seen & { kindOf: "#Spoiled" } @family(seen)
spoiled_look: #Look & { kindOf: "#Spoiled", look: "food.spoiled" } @family(looks)

// Its mass is what spoiled, carved from it.
spoiled_food: #Spoiled & { material: "rot", mass: 1g }
